  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "I am attempting to search for objects that have the string \"haven't\" in the description field. ",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "If I search for \"haven't\" as a terms search there is no problems. But if I try to search with a query like \"description~haven't\", I encountered the following problem:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "First the apostrophe character must be escaped as \\' to be accepted by the org.fcrepo.server.search.Condition.getConditions parser. (This is not a problem, but I am not sure it is documented)",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "But still with the apostrophe character escaped for the parser, the search condition is rejected by a check in the Condition constructor.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "If this check is removed, it becomes possible to search for the objects.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "I am attaching a diff file with the check removed and with added integration test that demonstrates the handling of apostrophes in terms and query type searches. It seems to work OK with this change",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "(This may also be related to ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "url": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/browse/FCREPO-867#icft=FCREPO-867"
       },
       "type": "inlineCard"
      },
      {
       "text": ")",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
